      "raw": "You can't really say you don't like movies, but you can absolutely say you don't like Bollywood movies.  Manga isn't just comic books, it's specifically the version of comic books done mostly in Japan; they have broad stylistic similarities within themselves with very few exceptions, so that's absolutely valid.\n\nWeird that super cheerful Christopher insists that Cowboy Bebop guy should be sad.\n\nWildheart should have been Wildrunner.\n\n\"America the character\" - now I want Legacy-san to arrive at the battlefield in a truck with a cowboy hat, finishing an enormous cheeseburger as he flies out of his truck to punch the villain.\n\nThe letter from Wesley here is actually the first one, and he traveled back in time to write letters earlier in June about how he declared war on that month to take it over.  I love it.\n\nSchmrlock Holmes?  Mrglrghlrghmrg!  And, unrelatedly, Maerinyans are fish-frogs!  Nobody tell the Old Man, he'll make a whole big thing of it.\n\nA manga trope they never even touched on is cute monster pets, and the blob in the background is sorta adorable in its slightly creepy way.  I think they should separate Vanessa from it and then without her mind twisting it and being twisted by power stolen from it, this shadow ghost thing with the big smile becomes the team mascot.\n\nGood knock-knock joke at the end!",
